<title>USA: USDA's Glickman sees APEC summit boosting ag trade.</title>
<headline>USDA's Glickman sees APEC summit boosting ag trade.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman Wednesday said he believed the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) Summit would lead to improved international cooperation and expanded agricultural trade.</p>
<p>Glickman, who leaves Thursday for the upcoming summit in Manila, said he would join President Clinton in meetings with the leaders of China, South Korea, the Philippines and Japan.</p>
<p>&quot;These meetings will afford me the opportunity to urge, as the APEC process moves ahead, that the agriculture sector moves with it,&quot; the secretary said in a statement.</p>
<p>He noted that U.S. agricultural exports are projected to hit a record $60 billion during 1996 and that APEC countries will account for two-thirds of the increase.</p>
</text>
